{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Haddad. Can you confirm your full name and date of birth for me?",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 5.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thomas Kowaksic, May 3rd, 1981.",
   "start": 5.76,
   "end": 8.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thanks, Thomas. You're walking a little carefully there. What happened?",
   "start": 10.14,
   "end": 13.26
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, Saturday I was helping move pallets at work, and I picked up a box of floor tile wrong. Twisted, you know, felt something grab in my lower back, right side.",
   "start": 14.2,
   "end": 23.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Ouch. Where do you work again? Harbor point distribution.",
   "start": 24.94,
   "end": 27.96
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I'm a shift laid in the warehouse.",
   "start": 28.66,
   "end": 30.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Got it. On a scale of 0 to 10, how bad is the pain?",
   "start": 31.2,
   "end": 34.1
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Right now, maybe a 6. When I bend over to tie my shoes, it's like an 8.",
   "start": 34.88,
   "end": 39.7
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Does it go anywhere, like down your leg?",
   "start": 40.28,
   "end": 42.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "A little into the right butt cheek, not down the leg.",
   "start": 42.94,
   "end": 46.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any numbness or tingling in your legs or feet. Any weakness, like your foot dragging.",
   "start": 46.96,
   "end": 51.58
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, no numbness. Legs feel normal just the back.",
   "start": 52.12,
   "end": 55.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I have to ask a few important ones any numbness in the groin or between your legs like where you'd sit on a saddle No Any trouble controlling your bladder or bowels or trouble starting to pee?",
   "start": 55.4,
   "end": 68.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, everything's working fine there",
   "start": 68.96,
   "end": 71.1
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "any fevers unexplained weight loss or any history of cancer None of that Have you had back trouble before I",
   "start": 71.1,
   "end": 79.94
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "had sciatica on the left side maybe six years ago Did physical therapy and it went away completely, haven't had it since.",
   "start": 80.0,
   "end": 87.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good, what have you tried so far?",
   "start": 88.68,
   "end": 90.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Ibuprofen, two of the two hundreds a couple times a day, and my wife Agneska's heating pad. The heat helps some. I'm kind of worried though, a guy on my crew herniated a disc doing the same thing and needed surgery.",
   "start": 91.12,
   "end": 104.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's understandable. Let's take a look. Blood pressure is 134 over 84, pulse 76, temperature 98 .4. Can you stand and bend forward for me?",
   "start": 105.66,
   "end": 117.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "That's about as far as I go.",
   "start": 117.86,
   "end": 119.54
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, forward bending is limited by pain, about halfway. I can feel tight, tender muscles along the right side of your lower back. No tenderness when I press right on the spine itself. Now lie back. I'm going to raise each leg straight.",
   "start": 120.42,
   "end": 134.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Just pulls in the back a little.",
   "start": 135.46,
   "end": 137.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Straight leg raise is negative on both sides. Strength is normal in both legs, reflexes are equal at the knees and ankles, and you can feel my touch the same on both sides. You walked in normally, and you can walk on your heels and toes.",
   "start": 137.16,
   "end": 152.14
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "So is it a disc?",
   "start": 152.88,
   "end": 153.98
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I don't think so. This looks like a strain of the muscles in your lower back. There are no warning signs, so you don't need an x -ray or MRI right now. Most of these get a lot better in two to four weeks.",
   "start": 154.72,
   "end": 166.52
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, that's a relief.",
   "start": 166.52,
   "end": 168.7
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "For pain, take ibuprofen 600mg 3 times a day with food for the next week or so. I'm also prescribing cyclobenzaprine, a muscle relaxer, 5mg at bedtime as needed for spasm. It can make you drowsy, so no driving or running the forklift after you take it.",
   "start": 169.69,
   "end": 188.43
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Guard it only at night.",
   "start": 189.21,
   "end": 190.47
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Keep using heat and keep moving. Gentle walking is better than bed rest. I'll write you a note for light duty, no lifting over 20 pounds, through October 15th.",
   "start": 191.52,
   "end": 202.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "My supervisor will want that, thanks.",
   "start": 202.3,
   "end": 204.6
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "If you're not better in two weeks, come back and we'll start physical therapy. And if you ever lose control of your bladder or bowels, get numb between your legs, or a leg gets weak, go to the emergency room right away.",
   "start": 205.64,
   "end": 218.1
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, Hopefully it doesn't come to that",
   "start": 218.74,
   "end": 221.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I don't expect it to let's plan a follow -up in two weeks. Take care of that back Thomas",
   "start": 221.16,
   "end": 226.72
  }
 ],
